==Enemy==
Golem Sunfish works like a weaker [[Ultima Beast Naala]], cursing and briefly freezing cats with a three-part Long Distance attack in a longer attack cycle. Although the three hits add up to cover a massive area of 1,300 range, only the first hit has Freeze and Curse, which carries most of its damage but lacks the piercing range of other hits, and has a tiny blind spot that allows units with the range of most meatshields.

==Strategy==
The most dangerous thing about Golem Sunfish is the support it comes with, as even a brief curse effect can spoil the performance of your specialists if you push too far into its first hit. Its second and third hits aren't as punishing, but it will add up which will chip and eventually kill your backliners or weaker meatshields.

[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] is a valuable unit to use against Golem Sunfish, being able to freeze it for 6.67 seconds and thus buying more time for units such as [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] to chip down its health. Likewise, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] can also tank it with the Curse Immunity [[Talents|Talent]]. Just beware that Golem Sunfish is often used as support, so most units will not be able to reach it unless the other threats are taken out first.

