==Trivia ==
*In Jewish folklore, a [[wikipedia:Golem|golem]] is an animated figure made from earthen materials and built to serve its creator, typically a rabbi.
*Golem Sunfish's Japanese name, マンボロス ''Manborosu'', may be derived from 翻車魚 ''manbō'' (sunfish) and ロスト ''rosuto'' (lost, referencing how Golem Sunfish was "lost" under the sea until it resurfaced) or タロース ''Tārosu''/タロス ''Tarosu'' ([[wikipedia:Talos|Talos]], a bronze automaton in Greek mythology). It's also the same as the Japanese name of [[wikia:patapon:Manboroth|Manboroth]], a ''[[wikia:patapon:Patapon 2|Patapon 2]]'' boss appearing in the mission [[wikia:patapon:Patapon 2:Ancient Guardian Manboroth|Ancient Guardian Manboroth]].
*Golem Sunfish may have been inspired by the [[wikia:mana:Mana Fortress|Mana Fortress]] from the game ''[[wikipedia:Secret of Mana|Secret of Mana]]''. Both are advanced, [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] superweapons that were created by ancients using archaic powers ([[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] power for Golem Sunfish, [[wikia:mana:Mana (element)|Mana]] for the Mana Fortress), could cause the destruction of the world (according to Golem Sunfish's Japanese description), were stopped by legendary figures before the events of the game, and eventually resurface from the ocean depths for the player to deal with (the Mana Fortress specifically coming back from the [https://wikiofmana.com/wiki/Sunken_Continent Sunken Continent]).
*Golem Sunfish's attack animation bears more than a passing reference to that of the [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] unit [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%CC%BE%B7%AF%A4%CE%A5%DF%A5%A4%A5%E9%C3%CB Bōkun no Miira Ō] (暴君のミイラ王, "Tyrant Mummy King") from [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou]], only green with three bursts of light rather than yellow with five bursts of light.
*The sage who sealed away Golem Sunfish could be one of the [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage Enemies]], and may specifically be the one mentioned in the [[Uncanny Legends]] ending.
*[[Shachiko]], another aquatic Relic enemy, may have some connection to Golem Sunfish. Golem Sunfish was sealed to the ocean depths by a sage but resurfaced from the ocean floor, which is where Shachiko's Japanese description says it found the Sage stone it ate.

